# RedBench Controller UI Guidelines (v2)

These rules guide implementation of the controller dashboard UI. They codify current behavior and expectations to keep the UI consistent, accessible, and easy to maintain.

## Architecture
- Prefer vanilla HTML/CSS/JS; do not introduce frameworks or CDNs. All assets must be self-hosted.
- UI consumes controller REST only; keep business logic on the server.
- UI state is transient and stored client-side (localStorage) only.

## File Structure
- UI lives under [redbench/internal/controller/ui/](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/).
- Single entry: [index.html](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/index.html), script [app.js](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/app.js), styles [style.css](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/style.css).

## Polling & Refresh
- Default polling interval: declare `REFRESH_MS = 1000` near the top-level constants.
- Implement full auto-refresh with a single interval that calls both `loadWorkers()` and `refreshJobStatus()`.
- When the Auto-Refresh toggle is OFF, run a dedicated status-only loop at `STATUS_REFRESH_MS` that calls `refreshJobStatus()` only. Never run both loops concurrently.
- Pause all polling on `document.hidden`; resume the appropriate loop on visibility restore.
- Avoid duplicate requests: stop one loop before starting another.
- Maintain a small `failureCount` for resilience and future backoff; do not spam the console.

## Status Rendering
- Use `refreshJobStatus()` as the single source of truth for job state and UI control toggling via `setJobControlsState()`.
- Promote terminal states to the status panel using `setStatus()`:
  - `failed` → level `error`, include `errorMessage` when available.
  - `completed` → level `success`.
  - `running` on immediate recheck after start may keep the optimistic start message; otherwise do not overwrite.
  - `no_jobs` should not emit an error.
- Suppress flicker by caching the last seen `{jobId, status}` and only updating the status panel when either changes.

## Workers Table & Sorting
- Persist sorting in localStorage key `rb_ui_v1_workersSort` with shape `{ key, dir }`.
- Default sort: `id` ascending. Numeric compare for numeric columns; date compare for `lastSeen` if parseable; string compare otherwise.
- Update `aria-sort` on header cells and support keyboard activation (Enter/Space).
- When a worker is `busy` on a target that is not present in the current form, add a subtle `mismatch` row style and tooltip.

## Persistence & Toggles
- Persist form values in `rb_ui_v1_jobForm`; debounce writes (≈200ms).
- Persist auto-refresh toggle state in `rb_ui_v1_autoRefresh` using `'1'|'0'`.
- The Reset action must be idempotent: clear localStorage and restore the initial HTML defaults.

## Error Handling
- Use `fetchJSON()` with `parseErrorResponse()` which prefers `error` or `message` fields when present.
- When showing details, pretty-print JSON on a new line after the main message.
- Never swallow exceptions silently in user flows; surface actionable information via `setStatus()` with an appropriate level.

## Accessibility
- Ensure interactive elements are focusable; visible focus outlines.
- Use `aria-live="polite"` on the main status container.
- Modal dialogs must trap focus, support Escape to close, and Enter to confirm.

## Styling
- Reuse existing utility classes: `panel`, `panel-head`, `controls`, `status`, `muted`.
- Status/state classes: `info`, `success`, `error`, and worker states `ok`, `idle`, `running`, `failed`, `stopped`.
- Prefer CSS variables defined in `:root` instead of hardcoded hex.

## Extractability
- Keep API paths relative to the controller host. When introducing configuration, attach a small surface like `window.__RB_CONFIG__` and read from it.

## Constants & No Magic Numbers
- Declare and reuse UI constants at the top of the script. Current key constants include:
  - `REFRESH_MS`, `STATUS_REFRESH_MS`, `RUNTIME_CACHE_TTL_MS`
  - `DEFAULT_ASSUMED_LATENCY_MS`, `MIN_GOROUTINE_MS`, `MIN_PER_ITERATION_MS`, `MS_PADDING_LENGTH`, `OPS_PER_GOROUTINE`, `OPS_PER_ITERATION`

## Conventions
- LocalStorage keys are versioned with `rb_ui_v1_*`. Bump the version when schema changes.
- Keep all UI logic in [app.js](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/app.js) unless file size becomes unwieldy.
